  --xcheck "M|4.783e-26|mm5's Moebius tail at M 48 (fastmul6, ks 957, kmax 23, chord-free) from this point's h13 state resampled with Delta kept, against this M 32 tail of record: Delta +4.783e-26 at the end, of which the h13 re-converge at M 48 was +4.831e-26 (I1098-mm5/ladder/D360m48, raw 2f0c13001, final state blob fc3c4ebe, h23 pending -3.47e-27). It also differs in machine (M5 Pro against i7-12700). Its own k* stage at kfree 15 (gain 1.67e28) took F 4.83e-50 to 2.79e-75 and moved Delta by +9.10e-32" \
  --note "D 360 ladder point on dh610, fastmul6 (site_y: d368a0c0 kernel, Python 478e9d86, no inner chord steps): the jump (Moebius ks 557) and h5-h13 by ladder_point.sh, then the Moebius tail at M 32, ks 957, kmax 23 (ladder_tail.sh mob). ks_gate.py at the jump's state read 4.2e-50 at ks 557 and 1.6e-66 at ks 757, so ks 957 is past the 1e-64 bar. The Moebius values carry $F. Gain from gainq.py at kfreeze 15 on the final state (dh610)"
rec 432 $L/D432/release_ls_h23_D432.0000.npz $L/D432/direct_s.jsonl $L/D432/tail_release_ls.jsonl --start $L/D432/start.npz \
