  --note "D 432 ladder point on mm5, fastmul6 (d368a0c0 kernel, Python 478e9d86): the jump (Moebius ks 665) and h5-h13 (ladder_point.sh), then the Moebius tail at M 32, ks 1065, kmax 23 (ladder_tail.sh mob). The Moebius values carry $F. Gains from gainq.py on the final state (dh610): kfreeze 15 2.30e28, 17 3.75e31"
rec 519 $L/D519/release_ls_h23_D519.0000.npz $L/D519/direct_s.jsonl $L/D519/tail_release_ls.jsonl --start $L/D519/start.npz \
  --kstar 15 --gain 1.9745e28 \
  --xcheck "M|7.739e-27|the Moebius tail at M 48 (ks 1196, kmax 23, fastmul6 site_y on dh610) from the M 32 h13 state resampled with Delta kept, h13 re-converged at M 48 and h15..h23 released again, against the M 32 tail of record: Delta +7.739e-27 at the end (I1098-dh610/ladder/D519m48, its h23 pending +2.18e-27);machine|0.0|dh370 (i7-8700, dh610's Skylake wheel of fastmul6, Python f398e829 with --inner_chord 0) against mm5 (M5 Pro, native build, Python 478e9d86): the same Moebius M 32 tail (ks 1196, kmax 23) from the same h13 state (blob b5a40765) ends in the same final state, bit for bit (blob 2ef0b501 on both, I1098-dh370/ladder/D519x and I1098-mm5/ladder/D519/tail_mob). The two share the kernel source (d368a0c0) and the input, and differ in machine, build and Python (whose release_ls takes the same path chord-free)" \
  --note "D 519 ladder point on mm5, fastmul6 (d368a0c0 kernel, Python 478e9d86): the jump (Moebius ks 796) and h5-h13 (ladder_point.sh), then the Moebius tail at M 32, ks 1196, kmax 23 (ladder_tail.sh mob). No u check exists (the u tail stalled at h15). The Moebius values carry $F. Gains from gainq.py on the final state (dh610): kfreeze 15 1.97e28, 17 4.08e31"
